From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Almeida Barrios <gabarrios2006@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:54:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(audio): serve each group-call sender's timed PCM over
 native protocol 3

Protocol 3 is protocol 2 (same 28-byte header and handshake shape, "NZA3")
plus timed PCM of each group-call sender, flagged 3 (timed | mixed): the
call record implements meowcaller's MixedTimedAudioSink only for a protocol
3 lease, so a protocol 2 client keeps the participant mixer and a mixed
frame that races a lease change is dropped rather than sent to a client
that would let one sender replace the others.

The single eight-frame timed channel becomes a queue bounded per sender:
eight frames (480 ms) per SSRC, 64 in all, drop-oldest within the sender.
A direct call keeps exactly the old bound; in a group one talker's burst no
longer pushes the other senders' audio out.

CallAudioTransportOpenV3 is exported; the Python wrapper declares it, lists
the protocols the DLL serves (audio_protocols) and opens the highest one up
to the protocol asked.

Tested: per-sender and total bounds, protocol 3 handshake and flags on the
wire, protocol 2 refusing group senders, unknown protocol refused; the
existing protocol 1/2 IPC tests pass.
